## What to deliver

Build and rig the drone up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a floating core with a solar-hot heart, two
counter-rotating rings, and a beam emitter projecting from the core face. The
required interface is a caller-driven **`emitter_pitch`** joint that tilts the beam
up and down about its mount, the auto **`ring_left_spin`** / **`ring_right_spin`**
and **`hover_bob`** joints, and the three required animations you author on them —
**`ring_spin`** (the counter-rotating rings), **`hover`** (the whole craft bobbing
in place), and **`pulse`** (the emitter nodding). Produce **every** required part,
joint, and animation; you may add your own extra parts, joints, or animations on
top, but do not drop or contradict the required interface. When you are satisfied,
stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
